1.0.4-snapshot
  Perception trace, GeoTool, SoundTool, level scans and console test benches
    Perception, GeoTool and SoundTool are new tabs. The perception trace logs what the stalkers and mutants near you hear, see, remember, fear and pick as enemy.
    GeoTool shows what the game's place checks say at your spot, live in its window, and saves your notes with every reading to its file for the game run.
    The Main tab adds 4 scans and a timer queue watch, while the console commands add 2 arenas, a life pump and 2 animation benches.

  Main
    - Added Mutant scan, a periodic log of every mutant squad with its species, faction, online state, smart terrain and commander.
    - Added Level scan, a periodic log of the squads, smart terrains, stashes and AlifePlus squads on the current level.
    - Added World scan, a squad census by faction and by level, with online and offline counts.
    - Added Geometry scan, which logs smart terrain distances, stash density, base spacing and feature layout when a level loads, then periodically.
    - Added Timer queue watch, for the freeze where every timer in the game stops at once. This watch records the timer that broke the queue.
      If the game freezes, run_string tz_watcher.log_queue_state() names that timer.
    - Added the online or offline state to every squad callback line.
    - Fixed payload logging crashing on a server object, whose id is a field where the watcher expected a method.

  Perception
    - Added the Perception trace, with one switch per system, written to testzone_perception.log. The trace reads engine state only.
      A run with an AI mod on and a run with it off compare line for line.
      Hearing logs every event that reaches a stalker, with how loud it was against what he needs to notice it. The first event of each sound of yours lists his 3 memory lists.
      Vision logs when he starts to see you, when he loses you, and his detection progress. Memory logs what he saw, heard and took as a hit from you.
      Danger logs the danger he holds, what he does about it, and how far he moved. Enemy logs who he picks as his enemy, who he drops, and whether he heard you before he saw you.
    - Added Radius, All sound sources and Include mutants, which set who the trace follows and which sounds it counts.

  GeoTool
    - Added GeoTool. Its open key shows your position in a dosimeter's digits and every place check, live while the window is open.
      The checks are the nearest smart terrain and base owner, the indoor, roof and underground tests, emission and shelter cover, rain and sky light.
      A note saves the spot with every reading to the GeoTool file of the game run, and the text says when a check reads the spot wrong.

  SoundTool
    - Added SoundTool on End. It plays the game's channels, DiegeticDread categories, NPC voice and any .ogg on disk, and writes your notes to the SoundTool file of the game run.
      It names the game code that plays each file. Game replays a channel, a dread sound or an actor theme the way that code does, a new random roll each click, with or without the Diegetic mods.
      Every sound also plays at the ear or in front of you at a preset or typed distance, with a height and a falloff override, and shows its measured loudness and its own falloff.
      An MCM Mute option that holds through loads silences the soundscape, weapons and music while you listen. A playlist note above an entry shows beside it on the screen.
      It browses any folder and opens playlists of game paths, absolute paths or paths next to the playlist. Files from outside the game are copied into the sounds folder for the session.
    - Replaced the review players of DiegeticAmbience and DiegeticDread, and logged to testzone.log.
    - Added the sound trace. It logs every sound the soundscape plays, with its channel, its distance from you, the map and the weather, to testzone_sound_trace.log.
      A run on plain Anomaly, GAMMA or the Diegetic mods compares line for line.
      On a modded exe with the mix meter, every play line carries the mix loudness, and a loudness line follows each second.

  Tool windows
    - Changed AnimationTool, GeoTool and SoundTool into devices built from the game's textures, each with a screen color and keys that set it apart.
      Every tool has the same title row, a green lamp while it runs something, a red lamp when it stops, and an info key that opens its manual.
    - Changed the 3 windows to keep their shape on 4:3, 16:9 and 21:9 screens. AnimationTool docks right, GeoTool docks left and SoundTool sits in the middle.
    - Changed AnimationTool's posture to the pose and moving keys, and the selected motion now shows above the note.
    - Changed AnimationTool to browse any folder for a playlist, as SoundTool does. Its shipped playlists stay at the root.
    - Rewrote the manual of each tool.

  Development
    - Added the Development tab with Log level, Immediate flush for every TestZone log, and Reset to defaults.

  Remote
    - Added the Remote tab. With it on and the game started with -dbg, a Lua file dropped into appdata/testzone/inbox runs within a second and is removed.
      A file in watch runs on every load and again whenever you edit it. Each run writes its result to outbox, and stalker-manager testzone-send drops a file and prints the result.
    - Added tz_remote.load_module, which swaps a loaded script for its edited source in the running game, with no restart and no reload of the save.
      It removes the old script's callbacks and timers first, so nothing runs twice, and it names the other scripts that still hold the old copy.
    - Added tz_remote.load_all_scripts, which reloads every script of every mod from disk by saving the game and loading that save a second later.

  Console commands
    - Added tz_commands for testing and filming, run through run_string in debug mode.
      The stalker arena keeps NPCs of 2 factions fighting on a ring. The mutant arena sends waves of mutants at you. Both arenas write testzone_arena.log.
      If you need to stay alive, the life pump holds your health, stamina and psy health up and damps every hit.
      The actor drive holds you in place or circles you, while the actor aim turns you to a mutant.
      You also get kits, spawns, weather, time, teleports to a smart terrain or a stash, and the unlocks for the north and fast travel in the same set.
    - Added the stroll, which tours a route with nobody at the keys: every outdoor level in each of its 10 weathers, then every underground level.
      At each stop it clears the creatures, sets the hour and weather, holds them for the time you give, and logs each stop to testzone_stroll.log.
      It turns on god mode and turns off the key press after a load, emissions and psi storms, and stop_stroll puts every one of them back.
    - Added tz_anim, an animation bench that plays a motion on the HUD, a mutant or an NPC, then logs whether it played.
    - Added AnimationTool on PgDn, a key MCM can change. This tool forces each candidate motion on the stalker you aim at, offers a prop picker, and logs your call on each motion.
    - Added tz_fx, console cyclers for post-process effects and ambient sound loops.
    - Added tz_loadgen, a profiler fixture of 30 load cases. check_capture() reads the last JitProfiler capture and marks each case caught, missed or inconclusive.

  General
    - Added the modded exes check. The game stops at load with a message when it finds neither demonized 20250908 or newer nor AOEngine.
    - Added a banner and the mod version to the MCM. The log names the mod, xlibs and exe versions at startup.
    - Fixed the TestZone timers in modpacks that replace the vanilla timer queue, such as demonized time events.

1.0.3
  An xlibs 1.2.3 floor, with newer xlibs accepted
    From this release the load check accepts xlibs 1.2.3 or any newer compatible version, where it used to ask for 1.2.1 exactly.

  - Changed the xlibs check to accept 1.2.3 or any newer compatible version. It used to stop the game on any version but 1.2.1.

1.0.2
  The xlibs 1.2.1 requirement
    This release runs on xlibs 1.2.1, and the load check asks for that exact version.

  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.2.1.

1.0.1
  The xlibs dependency check
    The mod now checks the xlibs version at load, and stops with a message if xlibs is missing or too old.

  - Added the xlibs check at load.

1.0.0
  AlifeLogger renamed to TestZone, the callback watcher and the profiler
    TestZone is the new name of AlifeLogger. The watcher logs every engine callback, while the profiler times suspect GAMMA functions.

  - Changed the name AlifeLogger to TestZone. The log is now testzone.log, and the MCM id is tz.
